Git author addresses
--------------------

Part of this repository's commit history carries the author address
`juergen.hahn@core-sensing.de` instead of the author's personal address.

This is a Git misconfiguration, not a statement about ownership. The address
belonged to an employer of the author at the time and was left configured
globally on a shared workstation, so it was applied to commits in this
repository as well as to unrelated work. Commits bearing that address were
written by the same author, on the same personal time and equipment, as every
other commit here.

The history has deliberately not been rewritten: the record is left intact and
this statement is recorded instead. The record supports the above. Of the 1285
commits in this repository as of this date, 666 (52%) were authored after 19:00
and 429 (33%) on a Saturday or Sunday; 235 (18%) fall within Monday-to-Friday
09:00-17:00. The 181 commits carrying the `core-sensing.de` address are
distributed across weekday and time of day in the same proportion as the
repository as a whole — also 18% within those hours. The address correlates with
nothing, which is the signature of a misconfigured global Git identity.

As of this date the repository's local Git configuration pins the author
identity to the personal address, so the misconfiguration cannot recur.

